  "id": "modern_taarab_mipasho",
  "name": "Modern taarab (Dar es Salaam mipasho keyboard taarab)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Dance-oriented taarab that took shape in Dar es Salaam in the 1990s, when troupes such as TOT Taarab and Muungano Cultural Troupe replaced much of the orchestral ensemble with electronic keyboards, electric guitar, bass and drums. Its songs, often called mipasho or rusha roho, trade pointed, teasing lyrics between rival singers and groups, and later bands such as Jahazi Modern Taarab carried the style through the 2000s.",
  "recipe": "classic mid-1990s modern taarab, functional Song, African pop branch. electronic keyboard credited drums unspecified, single coil electric guitar, electric bass. live tracking. tube condenser, 500-series boutique pre, brick-wall limiter, dynamic EQ. 24-bit digital plate reverb digital delay pitch shifter.",
